{"title":"2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c7cc583137cd786583f9df893ce7124f6b20e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$784$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd8372a707439157b6b8c15fa8575c97c23fcc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times2\\times2\\times2\\times7\\times7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2ac887c9c858cab708070212612e94e9c94fe0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4\\times7^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c7cc583137cd786583f9df893ce7124f6b20e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$784$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is a perfect square because it can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/0220710f0e48b70956e37d6e73ad13843e3c7f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^2\\times7)\\times(2^2\\times7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" />. The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d9294f6bf4b6ddca3666a028ddfd16372a4ba00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2\\times5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is not a perfect square. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70ce30269e2ac08802b847f6c4a0c53370077a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45\\times5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> is a perfect square since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550ee59c9912f47bc0a66038209c08a412ab2fc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45\\times5=3^2\\times5^2=(3\\times5)\\times(3\\times5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"286\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Parts\">Parts</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Parts\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3a (page does not exist)\">2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3a</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3b&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3b (page does not exist)\">2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3b</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3c&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3c (page does not exist)\">2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3c</a></li></ul>\n\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018025732\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count